      "text": "India to Conduct Extensive Tests Before Considering Ethanol Blending Beyond E20\n\nIndia will undertake extensive testing and develop the necessary supporting ecosystem before considering an increase in ethanol blending in petrol beyond the current 20% level, Union Petroleum and Natural Gas Minister Hardeep Singh Puri said, according to The Telegraph.\n\nSpeaking at a Constitution Day event at Devi Ahilya University in Indore, Puri said India had achieved its 20% ethanol blending target ahead of the original 2030 deadline.\n\nHe added that any move towards E25 or higher ethanol blending would depend on test results and the readiness of the supporting ecosystem.\n\nRead the full article here🔗\nhttps://t.co/KoiPLaKjVd\n\n#ChiniMandi #ChiniMandiUpdates #EthanolBlending #E20Petrol #EthanolPolicy \n\n@HardeepSPuri",
